message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Turning weight-space programming on its head"
abstract: >-
  What is a language model reading when it names a small network from its weights? Reads of small
  game-playing networks by six language models under a range of prompts, with turned boards, permuted
  inputs, destroyed weights and mixed layers: the write-up, the data and the code.
